The '''Prehistoric Island''' is a [[Sea Events|sea event]]. It is essential for obtaining the [[Dragonheart]], [[Dragonstorm]], [[Dino Hood]], [[T-Rex Skull]], [[Draco]] race and [[Draco#Version_4|its Race Awakening]], [[Dragon Egg]] and at an extremely rare chance, the [[Dragon]] fruit. It is widely renowned for being a rare [[Sea Events|sea event]].

==Spawning==
To spawn the Prehistoric Island, players need to sail into [[Sea Danger Level]] 6 ({{Color|8c00ff|'''????'''}}) and continue exploring until the island appears. The island can spawn even if the player in the boat does not have the [[Volcanic Magnet]], but having it increases the chances of the island spawning drastically. Thus, it is recommended for at least one player to have a [[Volcanic Magnet]] in the sea exploration group if they're hunting for the Prehistoric Island.

==Notes==
* The player can spawn it alone and the [[Volcano Event]] can be completed alone. (Not recommended.)
* The Prehistoric Island will despawn after all players leave the island.
* The Prehistoric Island can spawn at any time, regardless of whether it is day or night. However, it is recommended to attempt spawning during the day for better visibility and navigation.
* The Prehistoric Island can be spawned without a Volcanic Magnet, at a lower chance.
** As long as one player in the ship has a Volcanic Magnet, the island will have higher rates of spawning. The driver doesn't need to specifically have one in their [[inventory]], and neither do all players need to have one in theirs.
* Any player not nearby the island (not close enough to initiate the raid timer) when the [[Ancient Relic]] is interacted with, will be unable to collect any {{Dinosaur Bones}}[[Dinosaur Bones]] or a {{Dragon Egg}}[[Dragon Egg]], even if they have significantly contributed to the event.

==Usage==
The Prehistoric Island is the only location where the [[Fossil Expert]] can appear. The [[Fossil Expert]] enables players to use [[Dinosaur Bones]] the player gains from the [[Volcano Event]] to craft unique [[Accessories]], such as the [[T-Rex Skull]] and [[Dino Hood]].

Interacting with the '''Fossil Ancient Relic''' (not to be confused with [[Ancient Relic]]) triggers a cutscene, after which the [[Volcano Event]] begins. Said relic is the large T-Rex Skull on the ground in front of the volcano. 

The player has a very low chance of getting an east or west variant of the [[Dragon|Dragon Fruit]] by picking up the [[Dragon Egg|Dragon Egg]].

The player can find the [[Dragon Egg]] next to the '''Fossil Ancient Relic''', an item that is used to get the [[Draco]] [[race]], crafting weapons, or unlocking {{Mythical|}} [[Skins|Dragon skin]] recipes. The player will need to talk to the [[Dragon Wizard]] and learn the [[Dragon Tether]] ability to be able to grab the egg.

[[Dragon Egg]]s will not spawn if the relics health is under 90% once the event ends.

There is the [[Prehistoric Cave]] located under [[Fossil Expert]], where players with [[Draco]] can obtain its V4 and upgrade it. However, the cave will be closed until the [[Volcano Event]] is completed. Only one player can go inside and do the [[Trial of Flames]] per island.

==Volcano Event==
The '''Ancient Relic''' (or fossil) must be interacted with to start the event. The player has 5 minutes to complete the event, there are two main themes in this event:
# Players must keep the volcano pressure down by using moves with [[Destructible Physics]] and damage on the orange effects/flames on the volcano to destroy them.
# Protect the relic, which will be attacked by [[Lava Golem]]s. Players must protect the relic by preventing the [[Lava Golem]]s from hitting and destroying it.

These two events will occur simultaneously, so it is recommended to have two groups, one maintaining the volcano pressure and the other protecting the relic. However, it is fine for one player for each. Otherwise, it is very hard to solo.

When the timer runs out, players will be able to pick up as many bones as they can as quickly as possible on the ground near the relic. (The amount of bones spawn depends on how many players on the island when the event start, each player should spawn five bones). The black door will also open in a cave, but the player has to be using the [[Draco]] race to unlock it.

After the '''Volcano Event''' is completed, the entrance to the [[Trial of Flames]] cave on the island will be opened.

If the relic's [[health]] gets depleted, a message will appear stating "'''The relic has been fully destroyed'''", and all players who participated in the event will die, regardless of their health.

==Tips & Tricks==
* Simply consuming 4 [[Lava Potion|Lava Potions]] prior to the event starting makes it extremely easy, providing free range of movement with no risks whatsoever.
* A good strategy is spawning the Prehistoric Island with a single boat and someone driving it that has the [[Volcanic Magnet]] and that preferably has the [[Portal]] fruit equipped, to make [[Terrorshark]]s and all [[Sea Danger Level]] 6 ('''<font color="8c00ff">????</font>''') [[Sea Events]] despawn, with the Portal's [[Dimensional Rift]] [V] move. Once the Prehistoric Island spawns, open a portal at  [[Tiki Outpost]]; without going into the portal itself using mobility moves. Teleport 2-3 allied players to the island and, upon completing the '''Volcano Event''', the Volcano will drop 5x [[Dinosaur Bones]] per person on the island.
* Another good strategy is to fly above all [[Sea Events]] using [[The Sentinel]] with a small group of people (2-8 players recommended) all having a [[Volcanic Magnet]] in their inventory. Once the Prehistoric Island spawns, clear the '''Volcano Event''' and obtain 5x [[Dinosaur Bones]] per player that joined the event.
* It is recommended to split into two groups: one focuses on reducing the pressure of the volcano, while the other deals with eliminating the lava golems.
* A group of at least two people or more is recommended. If the player has only one friend or teammate, just get the player with the more explosive moves to handle the volcano pressure whilst the other fends off the lava golems.
* It is advisable to use a fruit with a flight ability like [[Eagle]] with [[Skull Guitar]], [[Light]] or [[Magma]] to quickly fly around the volcano and reduce the pressure in a short period of time.
* To better get rid of the golems that spawn, it is recommended to use moves with [[stun]], [[AoE]], and no cast animations so the player can swiftly avoid getting hit and lure the golems away from the relic, while killing the golems quickly.
* The best method to solo Prehistoric Island is to make use of [[Creation]]'s build mode to build a wall to protect the relic. This will eliminate the threat of [[Lava Golem]]s, allowing the player to fully focus on maintaining the pressure down. The player should keep in mind walls cannot be too close to the relic, otherwise the Lava Golems will be able to attack through it.
* Awakened [[Buddha]] is also viable to solo Prehistoric Island as the awakened '''[C]''' '''Light of Annihilation''' move's range can almost cover the frontside of the volcano. This allows the player to keep the pressure down without moving a lot while dealing with the [[Lava Golem]]s. Make sure to use movement moves to quickly move around the island if the cracks appear on the backside of the volcano.
* Players can use '''Scorching Donut [F]''' with Awakened [[Dough]] to easily traverse the Volcano to keep the volcano pressure down.
* Be careful when trying to patch orange effects on the near peak of the volcano as there is still lava on the sides and top of it.
* If the player doesn't have any flight moves, [[Skull Guitar]] is recommended (does not require to max stat on it) due to its M1 having [[Destructible Physics]]. This is recommended for a group of two to four people if most of them choose to protect the Relic. 
* [[Cannon]] and [[Bazooka]] can also be used in place of skull guitar if the player doesn't have skull guitar or any flight moves.
* A [[Sea Exploration Group|sea exploration group]] of at least two people is highly recommended for the Prehistoric Island; preferably at least a [[Buddha]] user with a sword for [[Lava Golem]]s and a player with a [[flight]] ability (like [[Phoenix]]'s or [[Dragon]]'s F ability) can be used on the volcano pressure. With this strategy, the [[Volcano Event]] can be easily beaten.
* One strategy any [[Dragon]] user could use to easily solo the Volcano Event is to keep alternating between [[Dragon|hybrid and full form]] to kill the golems with hybrid M1s and seal the volcano cracks with full form '''Scorching Downfall [C]'''. Doing this, however, requires the player to keep track of their [[Power Meter|fury meter]] at all times.
* One way to solo the Prehistoric Island is to deal with the golems is to hit them towards the beach, this will keep them there and stop them from damaging the relic. Doing this will allow the player to keep the volcanic pressure down, but do make sure to check if any golems spawned.
* With two people, one using [[Buddha]] and the other using [[Dough]], you can assign the  Buddha user the role of dealing with the golems, while the Dough user traverses the volcano with its '''[F] Scorching Donut''' ability, maintaining the volcano's pressure. 
* If a player is using [[Buddha]] with [[Sanguine Art]] and [[Skull Guitar]], they can solo the event by spamming Sanguine Art's long-ranged M1 to keep the golems at bay and using the Skull Guitar M1 to destroy lava spots without leaving the golem area. 
* For pressure using [[Gravity]] is a very good option, as you can use its M1 while you are flying, and the M1s have destructible physics. The only thing to keep in mind is to make sure you are using the meteorite strike versions of the M1.

==Notes==
* If the player who spawns the Prehistoric Island leaves, the island will despawn even if there are other players on the island. The [[Lava]] on the top of the volcano quickly kills the player, even if they have [[Magma]] or [[Tiger]] equipped.
* The Prehistoric Island has no cooldown, and the player can repeat this event multiple times even in the same server.
* The number of bones that spawn after completion of the event corresponds to the number of players that are on the Prehistoric Island when the event has started. Once the event has started, any players that participate that were not originally on the island will not get counted towards the total rewards.
** If a player uses [[Portal]]'s Dimensional Rift after the event has started, the people brought into the dimension will not be able to claim rewards.
* If the player dies before the event ends, they will not be able to see [[Dinosaur Bones]] and [[Dragon Egg]]s.
* If no one is around Prehistoric Island, even if it just spawned, it will immediately despawn.
* The player can get either the East or West variants of [[Dragon]] when collecting a [[Dragon Egg]], but at a very low chance.
* The player can only collect '''one''' [[Dragon Egg]] per '''Volcano Event'''.
* A total of four [[Dragon Egg]]s are required to get [[Dragonheart]], [[Dragonstorm]], and the [[Draco]] race. However, five trips to this island in total are needed. (First trip to unlock the [[Dragon Tether]] ability and the next four trips to collect the [[Dragon Egg]]s, unless another player uses [[Portal]]'s C Move to bring the player back to the island after they unlock Dragon Tether, making it so that only four trips are needed.)

==Trivia==
* The Prehistoric Island does not have a despawn time. However, it will still despawn instantly if no one is on the island, or if the player who spawned it leaves the game.
* The volcano eruption is one of the [[Admin Abilities]], which is called "Draconic Incandescence of the Vermilion Firmament".
* The Prehistoric Island is commonly abbreviated as "PH". 
* The Prehistoric Island, and other "rare" sea events, were used to be spawnable in any Sea Danger Level due to the now-patched "12-player glitch".
* Before update 31.3, there is a bug where volcanic pressure and relic health doesn't show. Because of this, players would prevent the relic from taking damage entirely and destroying the lava as soon as it spawns.
* There is another ongoing bug, where the event does not start, even after interacting with the relic.

